 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SPD3000 guided hardware test\n",
    "\n",
    "Copy this file to `test_spd300.ipynb`, select the Python environment containing this checkout, and run the cells in order.\n",
    "The notebook imports the installed `siglent_spd3000` package, so its results exercise the actual driver implementation rather than a duplicate test script.\n",
    "Read-only cells come first.\n",
    "Later cells that can change instrument state are disabled by default, show their plan, and require an exact confirmation phrase.\n",
    "Disconnect sensitive DUTs, use a correctly rated load or meter, keep the front panel accessible, and stop immediately if an output cannot be disabled.\n",
    "The complete acceptance procedure remains in [`.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md`](.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Connection settings\n",
    "\n",
    "Edit only this cell to select the connection type and its identifier.\n",
    "Replace `<TYPE>` with the `spd.ConnectionType` member you are testing, such as `SOCKET`, `VXI11`, `VISA`, or `GATEWAY`.\n",
    "Use a power-supply hostname or IP address for `SOCKET` and `VXI11`, a complete enumerated VISA resource for `VISA`, or `localhost`/`host[:port]` for `GATEWAY`.\n",
    "The two commented connection-specific arguments explain when to enable them; leave both commented for raw socket, VXI-11, system-default VISA, or an unauthenticated local gateway."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "connection-settings"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from __future__ import annotations\n",
    "\n",
    "import atexit\n",
    "import json\n",
    "from dataclasses import asdict\n",
    "from time import monotonic, sleep\n",
    "\n",
    "import siglent_spd3000 as spd\n",
    "\n",
    "CONNECTION_TYPE = spd.ConnectionType.<TYPE>  # e.g., SOCKET, VISA\n",
    "IDENTIFIER = \"<IDENTIFIER>\"\n",
    "TIMEOUT_S = 5.0\n",
    "MIN_COMMAND_INTERVAL_MS = 100.0\n",
    "\n",
    "if \"psu\" in globals():\n",
    "    psu.close()\n",
    "\n",
    "psu = spd.SPD3000.connect(\n",
    "    connection=CONNECTION_TYPE,\n",
    "    identifier=IDENTIFIER,\n",
    "    timeout_s=TIMEOUT_S,\n",
    "    min_command_interval_ms=MIN_COMMAND_INTERVAL_MS,\n",
    "    # visa_backend=\"@py\",  # Uncomment only to force PyVISA-py for a VISA connection.\n",
    "    # token=spd.load_gateway_auth(\"gateway-auth.toml\"),  # Uncomment for an authenticated gateway.\n",
    ")\n",
    "atexit.register(psu.close)\n",
    "print(f\"Connected to {psu.model.value} through {CONNECTION_TYPE.value}: {IDENTIFIER}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Identity, capabilities, and execution settings\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell performs fresh identity queries and prints the parsed model information, feature flags, timeout, and command interval."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "identity = psu.idn\n",
    "print(json.dumps(asdict(identity), indent=2, default=str))\n",
    "print(json.dumps(asdict(psu.capabilities), indent=2, default=str))\n",
    "print(\n",
    "    {\n",
    "        \"timeout_s\": psu.settings.timeout,\n",
    "        \"min_command_interval_ms\": psu.settings.min_command_interval * 1000.0,\n",
    "    }\n",
    ")\n",
    "assert identity.model is psu.model\n",
    "assert identity.raw == psu.scpi.query(\"*IDN?\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Decoded system status\n",
    "\n",
    "`SYSTem:STATus?` is decoded into a typed immutable result containing the operating mode and CH1/CH2 regulation, output, timer, and waveform state."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "status = psu.system.status\n",
    "print(json.dumps(asdict(status), indent=2, default=str))\n",
    "print(f\"System version: {psu.system.version}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. CH1 and CH2 read-only checks\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell compares programmed voltage/current properties with live measurements.\n",
    "Power is queried only on models that advertise that capability."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "for channel, source in ((spd.Channel.CH1, psu.ch1), (spd.Channel.CH2, psu.ch2)):\n",
    "    values = {\n",
    "        \"channel\": channel.value,\n",
    "        \"voltage_setpoint_v\": source.voltage,\n",
    "        \"current_setpoint_a\": source.current,\n",
    "        \"output\": source.output,\n",
    "        \"measured_voltage_v\": psu.measure.voltage(channel),\n",
    "        \"measured_current_a\": psu.measure.current(channel),\n",
    "    }\n",
    "    if psu.capabilities.measure_power:\n",
    "        values[\"measured_power_w\"] = psu.measure.power(channel)\n",
    "    print(json.dumps(values, indent=2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Model-specific read-only checks\n",
    "\n",
    "Network settings and front-panel lock state are queried only when the detected model supports those queries."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "if psu.capabilities.network:\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"ip_address\": psu.network.host,\n",
    "            \"subnet_mask\": psu.network.subnet_mask,\n",
    "            \"gateway\": psu.network.gateway,\n",
    "            \"dhcp\": psu.network.dhcp,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Network queries are not supported by {psu.model.value}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "if psu.capabilities.lock_query:\n",
    "    print({\"front_panel_locked\": psu.locked})\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f\"Lock-state query is not supported by {psu.model.value}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Repeated-query stability\n",
    "\n",
    "Repeated identity and status reads help reveal stale, truncated, or mistimed responses without changing hardware settings."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_ITERATIONS = 10\n",
    "started = monotonic()\n",
    "for iteration in range(1, READ_ITERATIONS + 1):\n",
    "    assert psu.idn.model is psu.model\n",
    "    current_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        f\"{iteration:03d}: status=0x{current_status.raw:04X}, \"\n",
    "        f\"mode={current_status.operating_mode.value}\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "print(f\"Completed {READ_ITERATIONS} iterations in {monotonic() - started:.2f} s\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Read-only serialized batch\n",
    "\n",
    "This exercises the public raw-SCPI batch path and, when connected through the gateway, verifies that the two queries are submitted as one non-interleaved batch."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "batch = psu.scpi.execute([spd.Query(\"*IDN?\"), spd.Query(\"SYST:STAT?\")])\n",
    "print(batch.values)\n",
    "assert len(batch.values) == 2\n",
    "assert all(isinstance(value, str) for value in batch.values)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 8. Optional error-queue read\n",
    "\n",
    "Reading `psu.system.error` removes one entry from the instrument error queue, so this diagnostic is opt-in even though it sends no write command."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY = False\n",
    "if READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY:\n",
    "    print(asdict(psu.system.error))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set READ_ONE_ERROR_QUEUE_ENTRY = True to consume one entry\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 9. Confirmed CH1/CH2 setting and output test\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell is the main hardware-control test.\n",
    "It validates the chosen values against the detected model, reads and displays the current state, and performs no write unless you type the exact confirmation phrase.\n",
    "The default 1 V and 0.1 A values are representable by every supported model, but they are not automatically safe for an attached DUT.\n",
    "`ENERGIZE_OUTPUT` is `False` by default; changing it to `True` briefly enables the selected output and records live measurements.\n",
    "A `finally` block disables the output, restores its original setpoints, and then restores its original output state."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "TEST_CHANNEL = spd.Channel.CH1\n",
    "TEST_VOLTAGE_V = 1.0\n",
    "TEST_CURRENT_A = 0.1\n",
    "ENERGIZE_OUTPUT = False\n",
    "OUTPUT_ON_SECONDS = 1.0\n",
    "\n",
    "source = {spd.Channel.CH1: psu.ch1, spd.Channel.CH2: psu.ch2}[TEST_CHANNEL]\n",
    "original_voltage = source.voltage\n",
    "original_current = source.current\n",
    "original_output = source.output\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"WARNING: this plan will send hardware-control commands.\")\n",
    "print(f\"Channel: {TEST_CHANNEL.value}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Voltage: {original_voltage} V -> {TEST_VOLTAGE_V} V\")\n",
    "print(f\"Current limit: {original_current} A -> {TEST_CURRENT_A} A\")\n",
    "print(f\"Briefly energize output: {ENERGIZE_OUTPUT}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Cleanup restores output state: {original_output}\")\n",
    "confirmation = f\"APPLY {TEST_CHANNEL.value}\"\n",
    "approved = input(f\"Type {confirmation!r} to proceed, or press Enter to cancel: \").strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "if approved != confirmation:\n",
    "    print(\"Cancelled before sending any write command.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        source.output = False\n",
    "        source.voltage = TEST_VOLTAGE_V\n",
    "        source.current = TEST_CURRENT_A\n",
    "        assert source.voltage == TEST_VOLTAGE_V\n",
    "        assert source.current == TEST_CURRENT_A\n",
    "        print(\"Setpoint round trip passed.\")\n",
    "        if ENERGIZE_OUTPUT:\n",
    "            source.output = True\n",
    "            assert source.output is True\n",
    "            sleep(OUTPUT_ON_SECONDS)\n",
    "            print(\n",
    "                {\n",
    "                    \"measured_voltage_v\": psu.measure.voltage(TEST_CHANNEL),\n",
    "                    \"measured_current_a\": psu.measure.current(TEST_CHANNEL),\n",
    "                }\n",
    "            )\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        source.output = False\n",
    "        source.voltage = original_voltage\n",
    "        source.current = original_current\n",
    "        source.output = original_output\n",
    "        print(\"Restored the original setpoints and output state.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 10. Optional CH3 output test\n",
    "\n",
    "CH3 has no documented remote output-state query, so this test requires physical observation and always sends `OFF` in `finally`.\n",
    "Run it only with CH3 unloaded or connected to a correctly rated verification instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST = False\n",
    "CH3_ON_SECONDS = 1.0\n",
    "if not RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_CH3_OUTPUT_TEST = True after preparing CH3 safely\")\n",
    "elif input(\"Type 'ENERGIZE CH3' to proceed: \").strip() != \"ENERGIZE CH3\":\n",
    "    print(\"Cancelled before sending any CH3 command.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        psu.output(spd.Channel.CH3, spd.OutputState.ON)\n",
    "        sleep(CH3_ON_SECONDS)\n",
    "        print(\"Confirm the CH3 front-panel indication and physical voltage now.\")\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        psu.output(spd.Channel.CH3, spd.OutputState.OFF)\n",
    "        print(\"Sent CH3 OFF.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 11. Optional timer and waveform configuration round trip\n",
    "\n",
    "This test is available only on SPD3303X/X-E, overwrites one timer group and toggles one waveform-display state after confirmation, verifies both, and restores their original values in `finally`.\n",
    "It deliberately does not start the timer or energize an output."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST = False\n",
    "TIMER_GROUP = 5\n",
    "TIMER_STEP = {\"voltage_v\": 1.0, \"current_a\": 0.1, \"duration_s\": 1.0}\n",
    "if not psu.capabilities.timer:\n",
    "    print(f\"Timer commands are not supported by {psu.model.value}\")\n",
    "elif not RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_TIMER_WAVEFORM_TEST = True to prepare this test\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    original_timer_step = psu.timer.set(TEST_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP)\n",
    "    timer_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "    channel_status = timer_status.ch1 if TEST_CHANNEL is spd.Channel.CH1 else timer_status.ch2\n",
    "    original_waveform = channel_status.waveform\n",
    "    print(\n",
    "        {\n",
    "            \"current_timer_step\": original_timer_step,\n",
    "            \"planned_timer_step\": TIMER_STEP,\n",
    "            \"current_waveform_display\": original_waveform,\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    phrase = f\"OVERWRITE TIMER {TEST_CHANNEL.value} {TIMER_GROUP}\"\n",
    "    if input(f\"Type {phrase!r} to proceed: \").strip() != phrase:\n",
    "        print(\"Cancelled before writing the timer group.\")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            psu.timer.set(TEST_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP, **TIMER_STEP)\n",
    "            assert psu.timer.set(TEST_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP) == TIMER_STEP\n",
    "            if original_waveform is not None:\n",
    "                changed_waveform = not original_waveform\n",
    "                psu.output.wave(\n",
    "                    TEST_CHANNEL,\n",
    "                    spd.WaveformState.ON if changed_waveform else spd.WaveformState.OFF,\n",
    "                )\n",
    "                changed_status = psu.system.status\n",
    "                changed_channel = (\n",
    "                    changed_status.ch1\n",
    "                    if TEST_CHANNEL is spd.Channel.CH1\n",
    "                    else changed_status.ch2\n",
    "                )\n",
    "                assert changed_channel.waveform is changed_waveform\n",
    "            print(\"Timer and waveform configuration round trip passed.\")\n",
    "        finally:\n",
    "            if original_waveform is not None:\n",
    "                psu.output.wave(\n",
    "                    TEST_CHANNEL,\n",
    "                    spd.WaveformState.ON if original_waveform else spd.WaveformState.OFF,\n",
    "                )\n",
    "            psu.timer.set(TEST_CHANNEL, TIMER_GROUP, **original_timer_step)\n",
    "            print(\"Restored the original timer group and waveform-display state.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 12. Optional front-panel lock round trip\n",
    "\n",
    "This test locks the front panel only after confirmation and always sends `*UNLOCK` in `finally`.\n",
    "SPD3303C supports lock/unlock commands but does not provide the documented `*LOCK?` verification query."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST = False\n",
    "if not RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST:\n",
    "    print(\"Skipped; set RUN_FRONT_PANEL_LOCK_TEST = True to prepare the lock test\")\n",
    "elif input(\"Type 'LOCK FRONT PANEL' to proceed: \").strip() != \"LOCK FRONT PANEL\":\n",
    "    print(\"Cancelled before locking the front panel.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        psu.lock()\n",
    "        if psu.capabilities.lock_query:\n",
    "            assert psu.locked is True\n",
    "        print(\"Confirm that the front-panel controls are locked.\")\n",
    "    finally:\n",
    "        psu.unlock()\n",
    "        if psu.capabilities.lock_query:\n",
    "            assert psu.locked is False\n",
    "        print(\"Sent *UNLOCK.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 13. Tests intentionally left to the acceptance checklist\n",
    "\n",
    "Tracking modes require verified series or parallel wiring, save/recall overwrites persistent setup memory, network writes can disconnect the instrument, invalid raw commands deliberately alter the error queue, and forced link failures require external intervention.\n",
    "Run those cases manually from [`.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md`](.agents/HARDWARE_TESTS.md) rather than turning them into casual notebook cells."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 14. Close the connection\n",
    "\n",
    "Run this final cell even after read-only testing so another process can immediately acquire the instrument."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "psu.close()\n",
    "atexit.unregister(psu.close)\n",
    "print(\"Connection closed.\")"
   ]
  }
 ],
